## Intent

PROBLEM, observed 2026-09-23: the captain could not answer a captain's call in words - not on the artifact review page, and not in Bearings either. Firstmate's first diagnosis was WRONG and this body replaces it: the artifact page is not merely behind Bearings, Bearings loses the field too.

ROOT CAUSE, src/App.tsx DecisionCard (:1095):
The component has TWO MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE BRANCHES chosen by whether the call has a linked argument page.
- :1177, taken when 'argument && onReadArgument' - the call IS argued by a page. Renders an 'Answer now' toggle (:1120 'keyed') revealing OPTION BUTTONS ONLY (:1195). No free-text field, no 'Not now' deferral.
- :1208-1214, the fallback when the call has NO argument page. Renders option chips, a 'Not now' button with a date field (:1211), AND the textarea labelled 'Or answer in words' (:1214).
So linking a call to the page that argues it REMOVES the captain's ability to answer in words or defer with a date. The affordances are lost exactly when the call carries the most context.

The artifact review page (:2607-2626, section.decision-answer) is options-only as well, so with an argued call there is NO surface anywhere offering free text.

HOW IT WAS SEEN: the captain first reported a call not appearing on its artifact page; that was missing page evidence and firstmate attached it (page:task/qd-nm-flow-1/nm-flow). Attaching it flipped the call into the argued branch, which is when the 'answer in words' field disappeared from Bearings. The fix caused the second symptom, which is also the clearest proof of the branch behaviour.

'DEFER' WAS NEVER MISSING: the record carried all four options and both branches map every option. What he lost was free text and the dated 'Not now', not an option. Firstmate earlier wrote that dropped options would be a separate defect - that line is withdrawn; nothing drops options.

WHAT TO FIX:
1. An argued call must keep free-text answering and the dated deferral. Decide whether the argued branch gains them or the two branches converge on one card; say which and why.
2. Bring the artifact review page (:2607-2626) to the same answer affordances, since deciding beside the evidence is the entire reason a call is linked to a page.
3. Keep what the artifact page already does well: :2612 shows an existing answer, :2304 warns when options changed since the revision being read, :2308 handles a call with no recorded options, :2315-2320 distinguish staged, sent and recorded.

Do not change the evidence-ref matching in src/calls.ts:21-24; that is correct and is what makes the link durable.

App-side. Verify in both themes with chrome-devtools-axi 0.1.35, and cover it in the scripts/*.mjs page checks alongside the existing call coverage.

LINE NUMBERS REFRESHED 2026-09-25 against main 490ccf1, after PRs #10, #11, #13 and #14 landed and App.tsx grew to 2830 lines. Verified now: DecisionCard at :1095, the argued branch at :1177 (if (argument && onReadArgument)), the dated Not now at :1211, the "Or answer in words" textarea at :1214, and the artifact page decision-answer section at :2607. Treat every line number here as a pointer to be re-confirmed, not a fact: this file is edited constantly and the anchors that matter are the code shapes, not the offsets.

LATER, THE CAPTAIN DECIDED (stop-here): ship this first. Bearings does not yet show an answer sent in a page review until firstmate records it, so the same call could be answered twice differently; that gap is filed as its own task, qd-pending-answer-1, and is not part of this change.

## What Changed

- Bearings now draws every call through a single `DecisionCard` answer form: the options, a dated "Not now", and words that can stand alone or go with an option. An argued call still leads with its argument and folds the form under "Answer now". Before, linking a call to its page dropped free text and the dated deferral. A dated "Not now" now keeps the words written beside it, and it can't be sent until a day is picked.
- The artifact review page's answer rail uses the same form. A call with no recorded options can now be answered in words there too. The rail still shows:
  - the recorded answer
  - a warning when the options changed since the revision being read
  - staged, sent and recorded answers as separate states
- Answers stored with a review can now be words-only or deferrals (`review.rs`, `types.ts`, `note`/`defer`, with a shared `answerInWords` in `src/calls.ts`):
  - Option answers still go through firstmate's intake.
  - Words and deferrals go in the review message for the first mate to record.
  - An unrecorded answer unlocks while the call is still asked, and a call firstmate asks again reopens.
  - Staged answers show again when the review is reopened, and are taken back once the call is answered.
  - The most recent earlier answer is kept.
- `pnpm artifacts` (`scripts/artifact-review.mjs`), `scripts/calls.test.mjs` and the mock now cover answering by option, in words, and with "Not now" until a day, and AGENTS.md describes this.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

## Risk Assessment

⚠️ Medium: The change meets the intent: one DecisionCard with words and a dated Not now for argued calls, and the same fields in the review rail. But it widens the review log contract (worded answers, `earlier`, reopening after send), and it has a real rail bug where staged words don't show when a page opens with its review still loading.

## Testing

I ran the React UI under Vite with the app's mock host, and ran the existing `pnpm artifacts` Playwright check against it. That check covers every new scenario: argued calls in Bearings, the page's rail in words and with a dated Not now, reopening after visiting another page, a call still asked after its day comes, words taken back once answered in chat, and a call with no recorded options. All 305 checks passed, with screenshots in both themes. I also checked the argued Bearings card by hand in chrome-devtools-axi in light and dark, and sent an answer in words from it. The review.rs unit tests and `pnpm test` passed. I did not run the native Tauri app or the token-spending live test (`review_e2e_live_decision`), so the real firstmate intake was covered only by unit tests.

