<summary>⚠️ **Review** - 1 info</summary>

- ⚠️ `src/App.tsx:2663` - RailCall sets up its local fields from `current` only once, when it mounts (`useState(Boolean(current?.defer))`, `useState(current?.defer ?? &#34;&#34;)`, `useState(current?.note ?? &#34;&#34;)`). But ArtifactReview mounts while `review` is still null: App.tsx:252 runs `setReview(null)` and then an async `reviewGet` whenever the page ref changes. So when a page with a staged answer in words is opened after a relaunch, or after visiting another page, `chosen` is undefined at mount. The textarea stays empty and Not now stays unselected, while the status line says &#34;Goes with your review, for the first mate to record&#34;. Worse, `stage()` merges `latest.current`, which holds the empty note. If the captain then clicks an option or Not now, the staged words are silently replaced with an empty note. Sending instead sends words the rail never showed. The mjs check only covers going back to the same page, where `openArtifact` is never cleared and the review stays loaded, so it misses this. Fix: render the rail calls only once `review` has loaded, or key RailCall on the review being loaded, or re-seed deferring/deferDate/note when `current` first arrives. This also applies to the staged option&#39;s added note (`current?.note`).
- ⚠️ `src-tauri/src/review.rs:218` - Simplification: the change adds an `earlier` list to ReviewView (review.rs view(), summary() lookup at :1127, mock, types.ts `earlier`) and a &#34;You said in your review, &lt;when&gt;: ...&#34; blockquote in RailCall (`before`/`then`/`saidThen`, App.tsx answer-earlier). No intent requirement asks for this history of past worded answers. The intent asks for free text and a dated Not now on argued calls in both surfaces, and for keeping the existing staged/sent/recorded indicators. Letting a call be answered again while firstmate still asks it (`anew`) is arguably needed so a dated Not now can be answered once its day comes. The kept history and its display go beyond that, and they grow the log/view contract. Recommend removing `earlier` and the answer-earlier blockquote unless James wants that history.
- ℹ️ `src-tauri/src/review.rs:1081` - `summary().answered` and the rail now count only intake-recorded answers as final. An option handed to the first mate by a review sent before the app called the intake used to lock, and was shown in Bearings as &#34;Answered in your review&#34;. It now reopens as answerable in both places. That is consistent with the stated design, and the related double-answer gap is filed as qd-pending-answer-1. It is noted here only because it changes how existing review logs behave.

🔧 Fix applied.
